id: pm-ya7x55
title: "The positional-argument layer of the command grammar has no lexicon and no gate: 21 distinct positional shapes across 76 commands, and three commands declare an optional subcommand they refuse to run without"
description: "Grammar governance covers three of the four layers an agent must learn. pm-fs8q9x owns flags (one spelling per concept), pm-wt43zj owns nouns and verbs (allowlist and vocabulary), pm-hqa8g1 owns exit codes, pm-x4nn3z owns error codes. Nothing owns positional arguments, and the measurement shows why that matters: the 76 rendered top-level commands present 21 distinct positional shapes. 42 take none. The item id alone appears as required <id> on 13 commands and optional [id] on 4, so the single most common concept in the surface has two arities with no rule saying which applies. Subcommand dispatch has five incompatible shapes: <subcommand> [id] [target] (graph), <subcommand> [artifact] [base] [ours] [theirs] (merge), [subcommand] [name] (schema, profile), [subcommand] [id] [stepRef] [reorderTo] (plan), and [namespaceOrSubcommand] [subcommand] (telemetry, whose first slot is polymorphic). pm config takes [scope] [action] [key] [value], a four-slot untyped chain where position alone carries meaning. The declared arity is also not the enforced arity. pm schema, pm profile, and pm plan all render [subcommand] as optional and all three exit 2 when it is omitted, while pm telemetry, pm item, pm workspace, and pm config render the same optional notation and genuinely accept omission with exit 0. Worse, the two commands that honestly declare <subcommand> as required (graph, merge) refuse with 'Missing required argument subcommand', whereas the three that declare it optional and are not refuse with 'Invalid argument value' - a different error class for the same condition, routing the agent toward correcting a value it never supplied. Bracket notation is therefore unreliable as a signal, which is precisely the cost the simplification epic exists to remove."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:contracts",grammar,simplification
created_at: "2026-08-02T15:03:08.302Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-18T06:46:22.256Z"
