comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-02T15:03:08.302Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate check before create: read pm-fs8q9x (flags), pm-wt43zj (nouns/verbs), pm-hqa8g1 (exit codes), pm-x4nn3z (error codes), pm-pbyu (noun-verb ADR), pm-7i97c3 (command intent), pm-gy885b (closed value domains) in full. All four grammar-governance items scope explicitly to flags, nouns/verbs, exit codes, and error codes respectively; none mentions positional arguments in title, description, or AC. pm-gy885b covers value domains a refusal fails to name, which is adjacent but concerns flag VALUES, not slot arity - recorded as discovered_from. No existing n7rr child covers argument placement; the existing children all consolidate which commands exist, not how their arguments are shaped."
  "2026-08-07T17:13:34.757Z","harness:claude-code","Another instance of the subcommand-scoped positional requirement, found while measuring graph analytics 2026-08-07. `pm graph dominators --json` exits 2 with \"graph dominators requires an item id\" under code invalid_argument_value. It is a correct refusal and it is invisible from the declared arity: `pm graph --help` renders the id positional as \"Root item id (traversals, paths, impact, and dominators)\", so the requirement is carried in prose inside an argument description rather than in the grammar. Of the sixteen graph subcommands, four require the id positional, one requires a second target positional, and eleven take none, all under a single declared `[id] [target]` shape. This is the same class as the schema/profile/plan versus graph/merge divergence already recorded here: one command, several arities, and the arity a caller must satisfy is discoverable only by being refused."
  "2026-08-18T04:51:46.250Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-18: one coupled SDK/CLI/MCP tranche will make positional actions and recovery references contract-declared, executable, parity-gated, and discoverable. Scope includes generated contracts, public SDK types, CLI help and recovery, MCP aliases, assurance negative controls, documentation, temporary-workspace acceptance, and packed npm/Bun consumers. Duplicate check used the complete 2,521-item all-status corpus with zero omissions or truncation."
  "2026-08-18T06:29:31.904Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: positional grammar gate reports 158 declared and 158 observed executable destinations, 20 distinct positional shapes under the budget of 21, no inactive package omissions, and zero findings. Full literal coverage passed 7,540 tests at 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-08-18T06:45:41.690Z","harness:codex","Closeout evidence: the public grammar table declares 158 observed/158 declared destinations with zero findings, 20 positional shapes under the budget of 21, typed required/variadic/value-kind semantics, public SDK exports, and a persistent-regression negative control. PM-linked focused execution passed 13/13 tests; full coverage and the repository grammar gate passed."
